  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 9.7.0 - Binary content sniffing + digest auth + curl-accurate cookies\nFIX: Binary files served under a wrong text Content-Type (e.g. .xlsx sent as text/plain) are no\n   longer corrupted. Payloads are sniffed for binary signatures (ZIP/Office, PDF, EXE, images,\n   archives, OLE2) and NUL bytes, matching curl's write-bytes-verbatim behavior. Reported by\n   Massimo Braga - thank you!\nFIX: FTP binary downloads are no longer corrupted (bytes are read raw, text decoding only for listings)\nFIX: (#41) -b/--cookie values and manual Cookie headers now always reach the wire, and session\n   cookies no longer leak between unrelated requests. Like curl, no automatic cookie engine.\n   Thanks linv2 for the precise diagnosis!\nNEW: (#40) --digest, --ntlm, --negotiate, --anyauth and --basic are now supported. -u with a\n   challenge scheme performs the proper 401 challenge-response flow instead of leaking\n   credentials as preemptive Basic. Thanks linv2!\nNEW: CurlOptions.AuthScheme property + parser support for the five auth-scheme flags\nFrameworks: netstandard2.0, net472, net48, net8.0, net9.0, net10.0\nSponsored by IronSoftware\n\nDocumentation: https://jacob-mellor.github.io/curl-dot-net/",
